module gunbc.plans.declaration_acquisition

import std.types { List }
import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { h2, h3, p, li, ul, quote }

fn declaration_acquisition_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    quote(blocks: [
      p(text: "**What.** The named consumers (the required gate's entry `gunbc.witness.compiler_gate_workflow`, heal's `gunbc.heal_candidate_stage0`, regen's `gunbc.instruments.generated_artifact_gate`) compile through the v2 native route instead of the v1 seed, every name in them binds to its authorized declaration or receiver operation, and v2 loads only the declarations they demand. **Why.** Moving the tree toward v2: each consumer that leaves v1 shrinks the seed's load-bearing surface, and v1 refusing what v2 refuses lets the one required job block new seed-only names. **How not.** No census mode, no corpus-wide audit, no second loader, no investment in v1's `gunbc run` path (an oracle only), no CI job or budget change."),
      p(text: "This carrier states the outcomes, their obligations and their done-when. How they are realized is downstream and replaceable (`gunbc.design_ruling::plans_are_intentions_and_realization_is_downstream`): the work items carry it, and section 6 lists only first candidates.")
    ]),
    h2(text: "1. Boundaries with existing programs"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**The dependency relation is the demand engine's.** `gunbc.plans.demand_engine_program` owns `v2.std.dependency` `DependencyRelation` over demand identity and M2's derived dependencies, including completeness before independence (a non-empty not-derived population refuses). This plan consumes that relation at declaration grain for acquisition; it does not define a second one."),
      li(text: "**Runtime demand closure on v1 is `gunbc.plans.closure_consolidation` P4.** That phase owns the seed's run-path closure (host-keyed reads, the symbol index that keeps ambiguity and missing-name refusals). This plan owns what v2 acquires. Where both need the same declaration-grain relation, it is the demand engine's, consumed by both."),
      li(text: "**Validity of a produced result is `gunbc.plans.read_set_convergence`.** This plan decides what to load, not whether an earlier product is still valid."),
      li(text: "**Method and roster naming is the namespace program's.** Namespace-resolution design section 13 rules that receiver-inhabitant methods stay independent of imports and free calls bind to imported declaration identities, with no ambient prelude (`gunbc.design_ruling::optional_sugar_is_declaration_bound`). This plan conforms to that contract; it reopens none of it.")
    ]),
    h2(text: "2. Outcome N: native coverage"),
    p(text: "**Done when** each named entry reaches, on the v2 native route, the same semantic judgment the seed reaches over the same entry, revision and source roots: accepted where the seed accepts and the acceptance is correct, refused with a located, typed cause where it refuses or where the seed's acceptance is a recorded seed defect. Successful emit is a step, not the criterion: emitted behavior, symbol bindings, refusal behavior and runtime semantics are compared at the entry's executing consumer."),
    p(text: "**Known refusals at main `6057af3a6219`** (first refusal per entry only; emit stops at the first module that fails to front-end):"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "Gate: `std.effect_grant` refuses `body_lowering_reason_paren_group_unread`. Located by probe: a parenthesised application in method-receiver position, `(skip(xs, 1)).first()`; `(xs).first()`, `(length(xs)) + 1`, `(a && b) || c` and the unparenthesised `filter(xs, v => p).first()` lower. The site is `std.effect_grant` `verb_of_label`; the refusal is raised in `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` `body_lower_paren_group_lowered`."),
      li(text: "Regen: the entry refuses `body_lowering_reason_statement_precedes_without_binding` at `run_generated_artifact_drift_gate_body`, an `if ... else ...` in statement position before `return verdict`. `body_lower_stmt_spine` admits only the else-less statement form; `let _ = if ...` lowers."),
      li(text: "Heal: `extdeps.cloud.gcp.gcp` refuses `body_lowering_reason_interface_member_unmodeled`, already declared as `gunbc.rung_drop.gcp_record_field_from_tail_unlowered_on_the_native_route` with its replacement and restoration trigger.")
    ]),
    p(text: "**Whether each gap blocks its entry is a question of demand, not of module membership.** Today's acquirer lowers every read module whole before resolving, so a gap in a declaration the entry never reaches still blocks it. If the declaration structure of a module (its declaration names, kinds and signatures) can be read from the parse before body lowering, a body-lowering gap blocks an entry only when the entry demands that declaration (section 4, D4). The gaps above are real either way; which of them is necessary for these entries is established by demand. Every probe that located a gap becomes a retained discriminating test with its positive control in the change that closes it."),
    h2(text: "3. Outcome B: naming convergence"),
    p(text: "**Done when** every name in the named closures binds to its authorized declaration (free call: an explicit import, or unique on the ancestor chain) or to its receiver operation (method: the receiver type's algebra template), on both routes, and no seed-only ambient lookup changes a program's meaning silently. **Per operation migrated, three witnesses:** an accepted case proving the intended declaration or template is selected; a negative case proving an unbound or ambiguous name refuses; and, where the runtime representation changes, an execution-level equivalence or an explicitly authorized behavior-change witness."),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**`first` is the first specimen, and it is semantic, not an import.** `std.algebra` `collection_first_shape` is its receiver template (`ReceiverSelf -> OptionalOf<ReceiverElement>`) and `std.methods` `first_method` its method declaration; v2 resolves `xs.first()` as the bare name `first` and refuses it unbound, which is v2 diverging from the receiver contract. Separately, the seed types `first` as `Optional<T>` but evaluates it to the bare element or `null` (`gunbc.recurring_failure_mode::the_ambient_first_evaluates_to_a_bare_value_under_an_optional_type`), so a site that compares, hashes, prints or serializes the result changes behavior when it migrates; and one operation already has three spellings (`gunbc.recurring_failure_mode::first_element_of_a_list_has_three_spellings`, `std.algebra` `list_head` among them). No new `first` declaration is added: the receiver template is the authority, and that failure mode's trigger is the consolidation."),
      li(text: "**Imports for free calls** go through `v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep` rows, not hand edits."),
      li(text: "**The seed's ambient window closes per verified population.** The built-in registry window that namespace-resolution design section 13 bounds by the generated import sweep #14017 closes only for operations whose three witnesses hold and whose consumers no longer depend on the ambient answer. Admitted under `gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing::v1_seed_standing` because it serves the self-host program: from then on the required job refuses a new ambient use of that operation on the gated closures.")
    ]),
    h2(text: "4. Outcome D: demand-grain soundness and efficiency"),
    p(text: "**Done when** v2 materializes only the declarations a named entry demands, every admitted dependency and refusal obligation is preserved, and the saving is measured against a comparable broader path. Soundness governs; efficiency is the measured consequence."),
    h3(text: "4.1 Unit"),
    p(text: "The module stays the unit of read (one exact read per module, R9; the read set is file-grain). The declaration is the unit of demand, keyed by `module.path::decl`. A type declaration is demanded whole, since exhaustiveness and inhabitance read every arm, and naming a variant arm demands its parent type."),
    h3(text: "4.2 The relation must be complete before anything is excluded"),
    p(text: "Selective admission is sound only over a dependency relation that carries every declaration a consumer reads, including reads the consumer's text never spells. Those are not only syntactic (a list literal's `std.algebra::FreeMonoid` head, `none`'s `std.optional::Absent`, a primitive's contract row, a service's realization siblings). They include semantic lookups whose selected declaration is chosen by a key: the 2026-11-10 incident in `gunbc.rung_drop.gunbc_run_unreached_declarations_not_realized` excluded a `CoproductWireContract` row that the interpreter finds by matching its `coproduct` reference, and the run could not decode a GitHub response. So: every implicit read, syntactic or keyed, is an edge in the relation before any declaration is excluded; an edge the relation cannot derive is a typed not-derived disposition that refuses selection (demand engine M2's completeness rule), never an omission; and a declaration that exists but was excluded, when consulted, refuses located as excluded, never reads as absent. The seed's realization audit and its known residual are the regression evidence this is checked against."),
    h3(text: "4.3 Verification at the consuming boundary"),
    p(text: "`v2.compiler.reference_closure` `reference_closure_ownership` keeps refusing `ReferenceOwnerless` and gains declaration grain: a resolved reference is owned only when its declaring path names an admitted declaration. That checks the resolver against the acquirer; it does not check the relation against the consumers. The second check is at the consumers that read implicitly (the keyed lookups of 4.2, inference, evaluation): each consults only admitted declarations, and a consultation outside the admitted set refuses there."),
    h3(text: "4.4 Checking contract per obligation"),
    p(text: "The seed's two declared losses have different populations and triggers and are not interchangeable: `gunbc.rung_drop.gunbc_run_unreached_function_bodies_not_typechecked` skips unreached function bodies; `gunbc.rung_drop.gunbc_run_unreached_declarations_not_realized` excludes whole declarations (signatures, type rows, data rows, module context). And the seed's claim runs keep full-closure checking where its demanded `gunbc run` does not. Before v2 narrows, the contract states, per obligation:"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Unconditional for every read module:** lexing and parsing; the module header (identity, layout row, cross-tree admission, import rows); acquisition's exactness refusals."),
      li(text: "**Conditional on demand, if admitted (D4):** body lowering, resolution and inference of a declaration nothing demands, explicitly or implicitly."),
      li(text: "**Which execution modes keep full-closure checking** (the v2 equivalent of claim runs), so that every conditional obligation is still discharged by some judged route, and which route that is."),
      li(text: "**Witnesses:** a reached declaration is checked; an unreached one is not loaded past its declared extent; an implicitly reached one (a keyed lookup) is admitted and checked; an excluded one consulted refuses located.")
    ]),
    h2(text: "5. Receipts"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Comparable or not at all.** A performance receipt compares the same entry, revision, source roots and invocation scope on both paths, and reports CLI build cost apart from command execution cost."),
      li(text: "**What is recorded:** modules read, declarations demanded, declarations realized, refused and skipped populations, wall time and peak memory, so avoided work is distinguished from moved cost."),
      li(text: "**In hand (not yet comparable):** srv1 (aarch64), main `6057af3a6219` re-committed in a fresh repository whose tree hash differs from main's (`a8769f49` against `1bcc3c1c`). v2 native CLI build: 25m09s, 3.28 GB. First-refusal emits: gate 2m33s, 352 MB; heal 20s, 69 MB; regen 0.8s, 22 MB. Seed regen through `gunbc run` (another session, after #16156): 3,398 modules in about 14 minutes. These locate the first refusals; they are not the baseline outcome D is judged against.")
    ]),
    h2(text: "6. First candidate steps (non-authoritative)"),
    p(text: "Work items carry the sequence. Candidates, in no binding order: emit refusals carry the diagnostic's locus and the acquisition receipt (modules read), which every later receipt needs; read whether `module_acquisition` can index declarations from the parse before body lowering (decides D4's premise and which gaps the entries demand); the method-receiver resolution divergence for `first` (outcome B); the parenthesised-receiver and statement-conditional lowering gaps once demand shows the entries reach them."),
    h2(text: "7. Decisions"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**D1, unit.** Module the unit of read, declaration the unit of demand, types whole (4.1). Recommendation: yes."),
      li(text: "**D2, method names.** Not open: section 13's receiver-inhabitant contract (section 1). The work is v2 conforming to it and the seed's `first` representation (section 3)."),
      li(text: "**D3, statement-position `if ... else ...`.** Recommendation: extend the else-less statement form to the conditional with both arms, keeping branch evaluation and the reference-conservation witnesses (`gunbc.recurring_failure_mode::lowering_accessor_collapses_a_sequence_operand` is the discarded-value risk both forms share)."),
      li(text: "**D4, conditional obligations.** Not decided. It is decidable only after 4.4's contract is written with its witnesses and the full-closure route named; a rung drop records an admitted loss and is not evidence that selective acquisition is sound.")
    ]),
    h2(text: "8. What this does not claim"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "The known refusals are first refusals per entry, not their populations."),
      li(text: "The implicit reads in 4.2 are a candidate set from source reading and one incident; the completeness obligation is the relation's, discharged by its not-derived refusal, not by this list."),
      li(text: "No corpus-wide count of ambient-name reliance is claimed or sought; outcome B is bounded to the named closures.")
    ])
  ]
}

data declaration_acquisition_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly,
  slug: "declaration-acquisition",
  title: "Declaration acquisition: the named consumers load through v2",
  body: declaration_acquisition_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Outcomes N, B and D hold for the three named entries: each reaches the seed's semantic judgment on the v2 native route, every name in their closures binds to its authorized declaration or receiver operation with the seed's ambient window closed for that population, and v2 admits by declaration over a complete relation with a comparable receipt. Then this plan deletes.") }
}
